          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of George Frideric Handel</strong><br>\nGeorge Frideric Handel was born in 1685 in Halle, Germany. His father was a barber-surgeon who wanted Handel to study law. Despite his father's wishes, Handel pursued music avidly from a young age. He became a skilled harpsichordist and organist and began composing by the time he was eleven years old.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Move to Hamburg</strong><br>\nIn 1703, Handel moved to Hamburg, a city famous for its musical activity and opera house. While in Hamburg, he played violin and harpsichord in the opera orchestra. He also composed his first two operas, \"Almira\" and \"Nero,\" which were produced at the Hamburg Opera.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Travel and Musical Development</strong><br>\nHandel traveled to Italy in 1706, where he stayed until 1710. Italy was an important center for baroque music, and Handel's style was greatly influenced by his experiences there. He composed several operas, oratorios, and cantatas during his time in Italy, honing his craft.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
